          "content": "# Anonymous Users - Implementation Guide\n\nGreat question! Anonymous users need special handling. Let me analyze your current setup and provide recommendations.\n\n---\n\n## **Current Anonymous User Flow**\n\nLooking at your `AuthScreen.tsx`:\n```typescript\nconst handleGuestEntry = async () => {\n  const { error } = await supabase.auth.signInAnonymously();\n};\n```\n\n**What happens:**\n- Supabase creates a temporary user in `auth.users`\n- User gets a `user_id` but no email/password\n- Session persists until user signs out or converts to permanent account\n\n---\n\n## **Issues with Current Setup**\n\n### **Problem 1: Profile Creation**\nYour trigger tries to create a profile for anonymous users, but:\n- Anonymous users have **no email**\n- Anonymous users have **no username in metadata**\n- They'll get auto-generated username like `user_12345678`\n\n### **Problem 2: Data Persistence**\n- Anonymous users can add favorites\n- If they clear app data or reinstall, **all data is lost**\n- No way to recover their account\n\n### **Problem 3: Conversion to Permanent Account**\n- No flow to convert anonymous → permanent user\n- User must start over if they want to sign up\n\n---\n\n## **Recommended Approach**\n\n### **Option A: Skip Profile for Anonymous Users (Simplest)**\n\n**Pros:**\n- No database changes needed\n- Anonymous users can still use app\n- Clean separation between guest/registered users\n\n**Cons:**\n- Anonymous users can't have usernames\n- Can't display \"guest\" username in UI\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Modify trigger to skip profile creation for anonymous users\n- Handle null username in app UI\n\n---\n\n### **Option B: Create Temporary Profile (Recommended)**\n\n**Pros:**\n- Consistent data model\n- Can show \"Guest_12345\" in UI\n- Easy to convert to permanent later\n\n**Cons:**\n- Slightly more complex trigger logic\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Modify trigger to detect anonymous users\n- Create profile with `guest_` prefix\n- Add conversion flow later\n\n---\n\n### **Option C: Disable Anonymous Auth (Strictest)**\n\n**Pros:**\n- Simplest - no special handling needed\n- Forces users to create accounts\n- Better for data retention\n\n**Cons:**\n- Higher friction for new users\n- Removes \"try before signup\" experience\n\n---\n\n## **My Recommendation: Option B + Conversion Flow**\n\nHere's what you need:\n\n---\n\n## **Step 1: Update Supabase Trigger**\n\nGo to **SQL Editor** and run:\n\n```sql\n-- Updated function to handle anonymous users\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()\nRETURNS TRIGGER\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nSET search_path = public\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n  is_anonymous BOOLEAN;\n  generated_username TEXT;\nBEGIN\n  -- Check if user is anonymous\n  is_anonymous := (NEW.is_anonymous = true);\n  \n  -- Generate username based on user type\n  IF is_anonymous THEN\n    generated_username := 'guest_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8);\n  ELSE\n    generated_username := COALESCE(\n      NEW.raw_user_meta_data->>'username',\n      'user_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8)\n    );\n  END IF;\n  \n  -- Insert profile\n  INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username)\n  VALUES (NEW.id, generated_username);\n  \n  RETURN NEW;\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN unique_violation THEN\n    -- Handle duplicate username\n    INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username)\n    VALUES (\n      NEW.id,\n      generated_username || '_' || substr(md5(random()::text), 1, 4)\n    );\n    RETURN NEW;\nEND;\n$$;\n```\n\n**What changed:**\n- Detects `is_anonymous` flag from Supabase\n- Anonymous users get `guest_12345678` username\n- Regular users get their chosen username or `user_12345678`\n\n---\n\n## **Step 2: Add Profile Table Column (Optional but Recommended)**\n\n```sql\n-- Add is_guest flag to profiles table\nALTER TABLE profiles \nADD COLUMN is_guest BOOLEAN DEFAULT false;\n\n-- Update existing anonymous users (if any)\nUPDATE profiles \nSET is_guest = true \nWHERE username LIKE 'guest_%';\n\n-- Update trigger to set is_guest flag\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()\nRETURNS TRIGGER\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nSET search_path = public\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n  is_anonymous BOOLEAN;\n  generated_username TEXT;\nBEGIN\n  is_anonymous := (NEW.is_anonymous = true);\n  \n  IF is_anonymous THEN\n    generated_username := 'guest_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8);\n  ELSE\n    generated_username := COALESCE(\n      NEW.raw_user_meta_data->>'username',\n      'user_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8)\n    );\n  END IF;\n  \n  INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username, is_guest)\n  VALUES (NEW.id, generated_username, is_anonymous);\n  \n  RETURN NEW;\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN unique_violation THEN\n    INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username, is_guest)\n    VALUES (\n      NEW.id,\n      generated_username || '_' || substr(md5(random()::text), 1, 4),\n      is_anonymous\n    );\n    RETURN NEW;\nEND;\n$$;\n```\n\n**Why this helps:**\n- Easy to identify guest users in database\n- Can show different UI for guests\n- Can filter/clean up old guest accounts\n\n---\n\n## **Step 3: Update RLS Policies**\n\nAnonymous users need same access as regular users:\n\n```sql\n-- Verify anonymous users can access their favorites\n-- (Your current policies should already work, but let's verify)\n\n-- Check current policy on favorites table\nSELECT * FROM pg_policies WHERE tablename = 'favorites';\n```\n\n**If you see policies using `auth.uid()`, they'll work for anonymous users too!**\n\nNo changes needed if your policies look like:\n```sql\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can view own favorites\"\n  ON favorites FOR SELECT\n  USING (auth.uid() = user_id);\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Step 4: Add Account Conversion Flow (Future)**\n\nThis allows anonymous users to \"claim\" their account:\n\n```sql\n-- Function to convert anonymous user to permanent\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.convert_anonymous_to_permanent(\n  new_email TEXT,\n  new_password TEXT,\n  new_username TEXT\n)\nRETURNS JSON\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n  current_user_id UUID;\nBEGIN\n  -- Get current user\n  current_user_id := auth.uid();\n  \n  IF current_user_id IS NULL THEN\n    RETURN json_build_object('error', 'Not authenticated');\n  END IF;\n  \n  -- Update auth user (Supabase handles this via API, not SQL)\n  -- Update profile\n  UPDATE profiles\n  SET \n    username = new_username,\n    is_guest = false,\n    updated_at = NOW()\n  WHERE id = current_user_id;\n  \n  RETURN json_build_object('success', true);\nEND;\n$$;\n```\n\n**Note:** Actual email/password update must be done via Supabase client API, not SQL.\n\n---\n\n## **Step 5: UI Considerations**\n\n### **Show Guest Status**\n```typescript\n// In your app\nconst { data: profile } = await supabase\n  .from('profiles')\n  .select('username, is_guest')\n  .eq('id', user.id)\n  .single();\n\nif (profile?.is_guest) {\n  // Show banner: \"You're browsing as a guest. Sign up to save your data!\"\n}\n```\n\n### **Prompt Conversion**\nShow prompts at strategic moments:\n- After adding 3rd favorite\n- Before signing out\n- In settings screen\n\n### **Data Loss Warning**\n```typescript\n// Before sign out\nif (profile?.is_guest) {\n  Alert.alert(\n    \"Guest Account\",\n    \"Your favorites will be lost. Create an account to save them?\",\n    [\n      { text: \"Sign Up\", onPress: () => navigate('Signup') },\n      { text: \"Continue as Guest\", style: \"destructive\" }\n    ]\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Step 6: Cleanup Old Guest Accounts (Optional)**\n\n```sql\n-- Function to delete old guest accounts (run periodically)\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.cleanup_old_guests()\nRETURNS void\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nAS $$\nBEGIN\n  -- Delete guest profiles older than 30 days with no favorites\n  DELETE FROM profiles\n  WHERE is_guest = true\n    AND created_at < NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days'\n    AND id NOT IN (SELECT DISTINCT user_id FROM favorites);\nEND;\n$$;\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Summary: What You Need to Do**\n\n### **Minimum (Required):**\n1. ✅ Run **Step 1** SQL (update trigger for anonymous users)\n2. ✅ Test: Sign in as guest → check if profile created with `guest_` prefix\n\n### **Recommended:**\n3. ✅ Run **Step 2** SQL (add `is_guest` column)\n4. ✅ Add UI indicators for guest users (banner/badge)\n5. ✅ Add \"Sign Up to Save Data\" prompts\n\n### **Future (Optional):**\n6. ⏳ Implement account conversion flow\n7. ⏳ Add cleanup job for old guest accounts\n\n---\n\n## **Testing Checklist**\n\nAfter running the SQL:\n\n1. **Test Anonymous Signup:**\n   ```typescript\n   await supabase.auth.signInAnonymously();\n   // Check if profile created with guest_12345678\n   ```\n\n2. **Test Regular Signup:**\n   ```typescript\n   await supabase.auth.signUp({\n     email: 'test@test.com',\n     password: 'password',\n     options: { data: { username: 'testuser' } }\n   });\n   // Check if profile created with 'testuser'\n   ```\n\n3. **Test Favorites:**\n   - Sign in as guest\n   - Add favorite\n   - Verify it saves\n   - Sign out and back in\n   - Verify favorite persists (same session)\n\n---\n\n## **Questions for You:**\n\n1. **Do you want to keep anonymous auth?** (I recommend yes for better UX)\n2. **Should we add account conversion now or later?** (Later is fine)\n3. **Should we show guest status in UI?** (I recommend yes)\n\n**Once you confirm, I'll provide the complete code changes for:**\n- Username field in signup\n- Forgot password flow\n- Guest user UI handling\n- Profile fetching\n\nLet me know which SQL steps you want to run, and I'll proceed with the app code!"
