          "message_id": "d2f40666-b9f4-4533-a9ff-c16e094fde6e",
          "content": "# Supabase Setup for Anonymous Users - Step by Step\n\nFollow these steps carefully to set up anonymous user support with conversion capability.\n\n---\n\n## **Step 1: Enable Anonymous Sign-Ins**\n\n1. Go to [https://supabase.com](https://supabase.com)\n2. Open your **StreamWatch project**\n3. Click **\"Authentication\"** in left sidebar\n4. Click **\"Providers\"** tab\n5. Scroll down to **\"Anonymous sign-ins\"**\n6. Toggle it **ON** (if not already enabled)\n7. Click **\"Save\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Allows `signInAnonymously()` to work\n- Creates temporary users without email/password\n\n---\n\n## **Step 2: Update the Profiles Trigger**\n\n1. Click **\"SQL Editor\"** in left sidebar\n2. Click **\"New query\"**\n3. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Updated function to handle anonymous users\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()\nRETURNS TRIGGER\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nSET search_path = public\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n  is_anonymous BOOLEAN;\n  generated_username TEXT;\nBEGIN\n  -- Check if user is anonymous (Supabase sets this flag)\n  is_anonymous := COALESCE(NEW.is_anonymous, false);\n  \n  -- Generate username based on user type\n  IF is_anonymous THEN\n    -- Anonymous users get guest_ prefix\n    generated_username := 'guest_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8);\n  ELSE\n    -- Regular users get their chosen username or user_ prefix\n    generated_username := COALESCE(\n      NEW.raw_user_meta_data->>'username',\n      'user_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8)\n    );\n  END IF;\n  \n  -- Insert profile with generated username\n  INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username)\n  VALUES (NEW.id, generated_username);\n  \n  RETURN NEW;\n  \nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN unique_violation THEN\n    -- If username already exists, add random suffix\n    INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username)\n    VALUES (\n      NEW.id,\n      generated_username || '_' || substr(md5(random()::text), 1, 4)\n    );\n    RETURN NEW;\nEND;\n$$;\n```\n\n4. Click **\"Run\"** (or press `Ctrl+Enter`)\n5. You should see: ✅ **\"Success. No rows returned\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Detects if new user is anonymous\n- Creates profile with `guest_12345678` for anonymous users\n- Creates profile with chosen username for regular users\n- Handles duplicate usernames automatically\n\n---\n\n## **Step 3: Add is_guest Column to Profiles**\n\n1. Still in **SQL Editor**, click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Add is_guest column to profiles table\nALTER TABLE profiles \nADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS is_guest BOOLEAN DEFAULT false;\n\n-- Add comment\nCOMMENT ON COLUMN profiles.is_guest IS 'True if user signed up anonymously';\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. You should see: ✅ **\"Success. No rows returned\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Adds a flag to identify guest users\n- Defaults to `false` for regular users\n- Allows easy filtering of guest accounts\n\n---\n\n## **Step 4: Update Trigger to Set is_guest Flag**\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Update trigger to set is_guest flag\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()\nRETURNS TRIGGER\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nSET search_path = public\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n  is_anonymous BOOLEAN;\n  generated_username TEXT;\nBEGIN\n  -- Check if user is anonymous\n  is_anonymous := COALESCE(NEW.is_anonymous, false);\n  \n  -- Generate username based on user type\n  IF is_anonymous THEN\n    generated_username := 'guest_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8);\n  ELSE\n    generated_username := COALESCE(\n      NEW.raw_user_meta_data->>'username',\n      'user_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8)\n    );\n  END IF;\n  \n  -- Insert profile with is_guest flag\n  INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username, is_guest)\n  VALUES (NEW.id, generated_username, is_anonymous);\n  \n  RETURN NEW;\n  \nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN unique_violation THEN\n    INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username, is_guest)\n    VALUES (\n      NEW.id,\n      generated_username || '_' || substr(md5(random()::text), 1, 4),\n      is_anonymous\n    );\n    RETURN NEW;\nEND;\n$$;\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. You should see: ✅ **\"Success. No rows returned\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Updates the trigger to save `is_guest` status\n- Makes it easy to identify guest users in queries\n\n---\n\n## **Step 5: Create Account Conversion Function**\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Function to convert guest account to permanent\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.convert_guest_to_permanent(\n  new_username TEXT\n)\nRETURNS JSON\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nSET search_path = public\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n  current_user_id UUID;\n  current_is_guest BOOLEAN;\nBEGIN\n  -- Get current user ID\n  current_user_id := auth.uid();\n  \n  -- Check if user is authenticated\n  IF current_user_id IS NULL THEN\n    RETURN json_build_object(\n      'success', false,\n      'error', 'Not authenticated'\n    );\n  END IF;\n  \n  -- Check if user is actually a guest\n  SELECT is_guest INTO current_is_guest\n  FROM profiles\n  WHERE id = current_user_id;\n  \n  IF NOT current_is_guest THEN\n    RETURN json_build_object(\n      'success', false,\n      'error', 'User is not a guest'\n    );\n  END IF;\n  \n  -- Check if username is already taken\n  IF EXISTS (\n    SELECT 1 FROM profiles \n    WHERE username = new_username \n    AND id != current_user_id\n  ) THEN\n    RETURN json_build_object(\n      'success', false,\n      'error', 'Username already taken'\n    );\n  END IF;\n  \n  -- Update profile\n  UPDATE profiles\n  SET \n    username = new_username,\n    is_guest = false,\n    updated_at = NOW()\n  WHERE id = current_user_id;\n  \n  RETURN json_build_object(\n    'success', true,\n    'username', new_username\n  );\n  \nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    RETURN json_build_object(\n      'success', false,\n      'error', SQLERRM\n    );\nEND;\n$$;\n\n-- Add comment\nCOMMENT ON FUNCTION public.convert_guest_to_permanent IS 'Converts anonymous user profile to permanent account';\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. You should see: ✅ **\"Success. No rows returned\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Allows guest users to claim their account\n- Updates username from `guest_12345678` to chosen username\n- Sets `is_guest` to `false`\n- Validates username availability\n\n---\n\n## **Step 6: Create Cleanup Function (Optional but Recommended)**\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Function to clean up old guest accounts\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.cleanup_old_guest_accounts(\n  days_old INTEGER DEFAULT 30\n)\nRETURNS JSON\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nSET search_path = public\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n  deleted_count INTEGER;\nBEGIN\n  -- Delete guest profiles older than specified days with no favorites\n  WITH deleted AS (\n    DELETE FROM profiles\n    WHERE is_guest = true\n      AND created_at < NOW() - (days_old || ' days')::INTERVAL\n      AND id NOT IN (SELECT DISTINCT user_id FROM favorites)\n    RETURNING id\n  )\n  SELECT COUNT(*) INTO deleted_count FROM deleted;\n  \n  RETURN json_build_object(\n    'success', true,\n    'deleted_count', deleted_count\n  );\n  \nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    RETURN json_build_object(\n      'success', false,\n      'error', SQLERRM\n    );\nEND;\n$$;\n\n-- Add comment\nCOMMENT ON FUNCTION public.cleanup_old_guest_accounts IS 'Deletes old guest accounts with no favorites';\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. You should see: ✅ **\"Success. No rows returned\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Removes old guest accounts (default: 30+ days old)\n- Only deletes guests with no favorites\n- Helps keep database clean\n- Returns count of deleted accounts\n\n---\n\n## **Step 7: Update RLS Policy for Conversion Function**\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Grant execute permission on conversion function to authenticated users\nGRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.convert_guest_to_permanent(TEXT) TO authenticated;\nGRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.convert_guest_to_permanent(TEXT) TO anon;\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. You should see: ✅ **\"Success. No rows returned\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Allows authenticated users (including guests) to call the conversion function\n- Required for the function to work from the app\n\n---\n\n## **Step 8: Verify Setup**\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Verify profiles table structure\nSELECT column_name, data_type, is_nullable, column_default\nFROM information_schema.columns\nWHERE table_schema = 'public'\n  AND table_name = 'profiles'\nORDER BY ordinal_position;\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. You should see these columns:\n   - `id` (uuid)\n   - `username` (text)\n   - `created_at` (timestamp)\n   - `updated_at` (timestamp)\n   - `is_guest` (boolean)\n\n---\n\n## **Step 9: Verify Functions Exist**\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Check all functions exist\nSELECT \n  routine_name,\n  routine_type\nFROM information_schema.routines\nWHERE routine_schema = 'public'\n  AND routine_name IN (\n    'handle_new_user',\n    'convert_guest_to_permanent',\n    'cleanup_old_guest_accounts'\n  )\nORDER BY routine_name;\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. You should see 3 functions listed\n\n---\n\n## **Step 10: Test Anonymous User Creation**\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Check if any anonymous users exist\nSELECT \n  u.id,\n  u.email,\n  u.is_anonymous,\n  p.username,\n  p.is_guest,\n  p.created_at\nFROM auth.users u\nLEFT JOIN profiles p ON u.id = p.id\nWHERE u.is_anonymous = true\nORDER BY p.created_at DESC\nLIMIT 5;\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. If you have existing anonymous users, you'll see them\n5. If not, you'll see: **\"Success. No rows returned\"** (this is fine)\n\n---\n\n## **Step 11: Update Existing Guest Profiles (If Any)**\n\nIf you already have anonymous users without the `is_guest` flag:\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Update existing guest profiles\nUPDATE profiles\nSET is_guest = true\nWHERE username LIKE 'guest_%'\n  AND is_guest = false;\n\n-- Check how many were updated\nSELECT COUNT(*) as updated_count\nFROM profiles\nWHERE username LIKE 'guest_%'\n  AND is_guest = true;\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. You'll see how many profiles were updated\n\n---\n\n## **Verification Checklist**\n\nBefore proceeding to app code, verify:\n\n- ✅ Anonymous sign-ins enabled in Authentication settings\n- ✅ `profiles` table has `is_guest` column\n- ✅ Trigger `on_auth_user_created` updated\n- ✅ Function `handle_new_user` exists and updated\n- ✅ Function `convert_guest_to_permanent` exists\n- ✅ Function `cleanup_old_guest_accounts` exists\n- ✅ Execute permissions granted on conversion function\n\n---\n\n## **Test in Supabase Dashboard (Optional)**\n\nYou can test the conversion function manually:\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste this SQL:\n\n```sql\n-- Test conversion function (will fail if not logged in as guest)\nSELECT public.convert_guest_to_permanent('test_username_123');\n```\n\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. You'll see an error (expected, since you're not logged in as a guest user)\n5. This confirms the function exists and has proper security\n\n---\n\n## **Common Issues & Solutions**\n\n### Issue: \"column 'is_guest' already exists\"\n**Solution:** Skip Step 3, the column is already there.\n\n### Issue: \"function already exists\"\n**Solution:** The SQL uses `CREATE OR REPLACE`, so it should work. If not, run:\n```sql\nDROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS public.handle_new_user() CASCADE;\n```\nThen re-run the function creation.\n\n### Issue: \"permission denied\"\n**Solution:** Make sure you're logged in as the project owner in Supabase dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## **Next Steps**\n\nOnce you've completed all steps and verified:\n\n1. **Reply with**: \"Anonymous user setup complete\"\n2. I'll provide the **complete app code** for:\n   - Username field in signup/signin\n   - Forgot password screen\n   - Password reset screen\n   - Guest user UI (banner, prompts)\n   - Account conversion flow\n   - Profile fetching with guest detection\n\n---\n\n**Take your time with each step. Let me know when you're done or if you hit any errors!**"
