                "command": "create",
                "file_text": "# Supabase Configuration for Auth-Only App\n\n## Step-by-Step Guide\n\nFollow these steps carefully to configure Supabase for the auth-only app.\n\n---\n\n## **Step 1: Disable Anonymous Sign-Ins**\n\n1. Go to [https://supabase.com](https://supabase.com)\n2. Sign in to your account\n3. Click on your **StreamWatch project**\n4. Click **\"Authentication\"** in the left sidebar\n5. Click **\"Providers\"** tab\n6. Scroll down to **\"Anonymous sign-ins\"**\n7. Toggle it **OFF** (if it's currently ON)\n8. Click **\"Save\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Prevents anonymous user creation\n- Forces users to sign up with email/password\n\n---\n\n## **Step 2: Enable Email Confirmations**\n\n1. Still in **\"Authentication\"** section\n2. Click **\"Providers\"** tab\n3. Find **\"Email\"** provider\n4. Click on it to expand settings\n5. **Check** \"Enable email confirmations\"\n6. Click **\"Save\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Sends verification email on signup\n- Users must verify email before full access (optional enforcement)\n- Enables password recovery\n\n---\n\n## **Step 3: Configure Email Templates (Optional but Recommended)**\n\n### Confirmation Email Template\n\n1. In **\"Authentication\"** section\n2. Click **\"Email Templates\"** tab\n3. Select **\"Confirm signup\"** template\n4. Customize the email (optional):\n   ```html\n   <h2>Welcome to StreamWatch!</h2>\n   <p>Click the link below to confirm your email:</p>\n   <p><a href=\"{{ .ConfirmationURL }}\">Confirm Email</a></p>\n   ```\n5. Click **\"Save\"**\n\n### Password Reset Template\n\n1. Select **\"Reset Password\"** template\n2. Verify the **Confirmation URL** is:\n   ```\n   {{ .SiteURL }}/auth/reset-password?token={{ .Token }}&type=recovery\n   ```\n3. Click **\"Save\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Professional-looking emails\n- Better user experience\n\n---\n\n## **Step 4: Configure Redirect URLs**\n\n1. Still in **\"Authentication\"** section\n2. Click **\"URL Configuration\"** tab\n3. Under **\"Redirect URLs\"**, verify these are present:\n   ```\n   streamwatch://reset-password\n   streamwatch://auth/callback\n   ```\n4. If not present, add them\n5. Click **\"Save\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Allows deep linking for password reset\n- Required for mobile app\n\n---\n\n## **Step 5: Set Email Rate Limits (Optional)**\n\n1. In **\"Authentication\"** section\n2. Click **\"Rate Limits\"** tab\n3. Configure limits:\n   - **Email signups:** 10 per hour per IP\n   - **Password resets:** 5 per hour per email\n4. Click **\"Save\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Prevents spam/abuse\n- Protects your email quota\n\n---\n\n## **Step 6: Clean Up Database (Optional)**\n\n### Remove Guest Conversion Function\n\n1. Click **\"SQL Editor\"** in left sidebar\n2. Click **\"New query\"**\n3. Copy and paste:\n   ```sql\n   -- Remove guest conversion function (no longer needed)\n   DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS public.convert_guest_to_permanent(TEXT);\n   ```\n4. Click **\"Run\"**\n5. Should see: ✅ **\"Success. No rows returned\"**\n\n### Clean Up Existing Guest Accounts (Optional)\n\n1. Click **\"New query\"**\n2. Copy and paste:\n   ```sql\n   -- View existing guest accounts\n   SELECT \n     p.id,\n     p.username,\n     p.is_guest,\n     p.created_at,\n     COUNT(f.id) as favorite_count\n   FROM profiles p\n   LEFT JOIN favorites f ON p.user_id = f.user_id\n   WHERE p.is_guest = true\n   GROUP BY p.id, p.username, p.is_guest, p.created_at\n   ORDER BY p.created_at DESC;\n   ```\n3. Click **\"Run\"**\n4. Review the guest accounts\n\n**To delete guest accounts with no favorites:**\n```sql\n-- Delete guest accounts with no favorites\nDELETE FROM profiles\nWHERE is_guest = true\n  AND id NOT IN (SELECT DISTINCT user_id FROM favorites);\n```\n\n**Warning:** Only run this if you're sure you want to delete guest accounts!\n\n---\n\n## **Step 7: Update Trigger (Optional - For New Users)**\n\nThe existing trigger handles both guest and regular users. You can simplify it:\n\n1. Click **\"SQL Editor\"**\n2. Click **\"New query\"**\n3. Copy and paste:\n   ```sql\n   -- Simplified trigger for auth-only users\n   CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()\n   RETURNS TRIGGER\n   LANGUAGE plpgsql\n   SECURITY DEFINER\n   SET search_path = public\n   AS $$\n   DECLARE\n     generated_username TEXT;\n   BEGIN\n     -- Generate username from metadata or fallback\n     generated_username := COALESCE(\n       NEW.raw_user_meta_data->>'username',\n       'user_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8)\n     );\n     \n     -- Insert profile (is_guest always false now)\n     INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username, is_guest)\n     VALUES (NEW.id, generated_username, false);\n     \n     RETURN NEW;\n   EXCEPTION\n     WHEN unique_violation THEN\n       -- Handle duplicate username\n       INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username, is_guest)\n       VALUES (\n         NEW.id,\n         generated_username || '_' || substr(md5(random()::text), 1, 4),\n         false\n       );\n       RETURN NEW;\n   END;\n   $$;\n   ```\n4. Click **\"Run\"**\n5. Should see: ✅ **\"Success. No rows returned\"**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Simplifies trigger logic\n- Always sets `is_guest` to false\n- Cleaner code\n\n---\n\n## **Step 8: Verify Configuration**\n\n### Test Email Sending\n\n1. In **\"Authentication\"** section\n2. Click **\"Users\"** tab\n3. Click **\"Invite user\"**\n4. Enter a test email\n5. Click **\"Send invite\"**\n6. Check if email arrives\n\n**If email doesn't arrive:**\n- Check spam folder\n- Verify SMTP settings (if custom)\n- Check Supabase email quota\n\n### Test Signup Flow\n\n1. Open your app\n2. Try signing up with a new account\n3. Check email for confirmation link\n4. Click link to verify\n5. Try signing in\n\n---\n\n## **Step 9: Configure SMTP (Optional - For Production)**\n\nFor production, use a custom email provider:\n\n1. In **\"Authentication\"** section\n2. Click **\"Settings\"** tab\n3. Scroll to **\"SMTP Settings\"**\n4. Choose provider:\n   - **SendGrid** (recommended)\n   - **AWS SES**\n   - **Mailgun**\n   - **Custom SMTP**\n5. Enter credentials\n6. Click **\"Save\"**\n7. Test email sending\n\n**Why custom SMTP:**\n- Better deliverability\n- Higher email limits\n- Professional sender address\n- Detailed analytics\n\n---\n\n## **Step 10: Set Up Email Verification Enforcement (Optional)**\n\nTo require email verification before app access:\n\n1. In **\"Authentication\"** section\n2. Click **\"Policies\"** tab\n3. Add RLS policy to `favorites` table:\n   ```sql\n   -- Only allow verified users to add favorites\n   CREATE POLICY \"Verified users only\"\n     ON favorites\n     FOR INSERT\n     WITH CHECK (\n       auth.uid() = user_id \n       AND (\n         SELECT email_confirmed_at \n         FROM auth.users \n         WHERE id = auth.uid()\n       ) IS NOT NULL\n     );\n   ```\n\n**What this does:**\n- Users must verify email before adding favorites\n- Ensures all users have valid emails\n\n---\n\n## **Verification Checklist**\n\nBefore considering setup complete:\n\n- [ ] Anonymous sign-ins disabled\n- [ ] Email confirmations enabled\n- [ ] Email templates configured\n- [ ] Redirect URLs set\n- [ ] Rate limits configured (optional)\n- [ ] Guest conversion function removed (optional)\n- [ ] Trigger simplified (optional)\n- [ ] Email sending tested\n- [ ] Signup flow tested\n- [ ] SMTP configured (for production)\n\n---\n\n## **Common Issues**\n\n### Issue: Emails not sending\n**Solutions:**\n1. Check Supabase email quota (free tier: 3 emails/hour)\n2. Configure custom SMTP provider\n3. Check spam folder\n4. Verify email template syntax\n\n### Issue: \"Email already registered\"\n**Solution:** User already exists, use \"Forgot Password\" instead\n\n### Issue: Confirmation link doesn't work\n**Solution:** \n1. Verify redirect URLs in Supabase\n2. Check deep linking configuration in app.json\n3. Test on physical device (not simulator)\n\n### Issue: Rate limit exceeded\n**Solution:**\n1. Wait for rate limit to reset\n2. Increase limits in Supabase settings\n3. Use different email/IP for testing\n\n---\n\n## **Production Checklist**\n\nBefore going live:\n\n- [ ] Custom SMTP configured\n- [ ] Email templates customized\n- [ ] Rate limits set appropriately\n- [ ] Email verification enforced (optional)\n- [ ] Guest accounts cleaned up\n- [ ] Backup database\n- [ ] Test complete signup flow\n- [ ] Test password reset flow\n- [ ] Monitor email deliverability\n\n---\n\n## **Next Steps**\n\n1. Complete all steps above\n2. Test signup flow in app\n3. Verify email confirmation works\n4. Test password reset\n5. Deploy to production\n\n---\n\n## **Support**\n\nIf you encounter issues:\n1. Check Supabase logs (Dashboard → Logs)\n2. Check app console for errors\n3. Verify all steps completed\n4. Test with fresh email address\n\n---\n\n**Configuration complete!** Your app is now auth-only with email verification. 🎉\n",
