          "content": "Perfect! Here are the SQL queries to completely clean up your database and start fresh.\n\n## **⚠️ WARNING: These queries will DELETE ALL DATA**\n\nRun these in **Supabase SQL Editor** in this exact order:\n\n---\n\n## **Step 1: Delete All Favorites**\n\n```sql\n-- Delete all favorites\nDELETE FROM favorites;\n```\n\n**What this does:** Removes all stream favorites from the database.\n\n---\n\n## **Step 2: Delete All Profiles**\n\n```sql\n-- Delete all profiles\nDELETE FROM profiles;\n```\n\n**What this does:** Removes all user profiles (username, is_guest, etc.)\n\n---\n\n## **Step 3: Delete All Auth Users**\n\n```sql\n-- Delete all users from auth.users table\n-- This requires admin privileges\nDELETE FROM auth.users;\n```\n\n**What this does:** Removes all authentication users (email, password, etc.)\n\n---\n\n## **Step 4: Verify Cleanup**\n\n```sql\n-- Check if everything is deleted\nSELECT 'favorites' as table_name, COUNT(*) as count FROM favorites\nUNION ALL\nSELECT 'profiles', COUNT(*) FROM profiles\nUNION ALL\nSELECT 'auth.users', COUNT(*) FROM auth.users;\n```\n\n**Expected result:** All counts should be `0`\n\n---\n\n## **Alternative: Single Query (All at Once)**\n\nIf you want to delete everything in one go:\n\n```sql\n-- Delete everything in correct order (respects foreign keys)\nDELETE FROM favorites;\nDELETE FROM profiles;\nDELETE FROM auth.users;\n\n-- Verify\nSELECT \n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM favorites) as favorites_count,\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM profiles) as profiles_count,\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM auth.users) as users_count;\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Step 5: Reset Auto-Increment (Optional)**\n\nIf you want to reset ID sequences:\n\n```sql\n-- Reset favorites ID sequence\nALTER SEQUENCE favorites_id_seq RESTART WITH 1;\n\n-- Verify reset\nSELECT nextval('favorites_id_seq');\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Complete Fresh Start Script**\n\nCopy and paste this entire block:\n\n```sql\n-- ============================================\n-- COMPLETE DATABASE CLEANUP\n-- WARNING: Deletes ALL users and data\n-- ============================================\n\n-- Step 1: Delete all favorites\nDELETE FROM favorites;\n\n-- Step 2: Delete all profiles\nDELETE FROM profiles;\n\n-- Step 3: Delete all auth users\nDELETE FROM auth.users;\n\n-- Step 4: Reset sequences (optional)\nALTER SEQUENCE favorites_id_seq RESTART WITH 1;\n\n-- Step 5: Verify cleanup\nSELECT \n  'Cleanup Complete!' as status,\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM favorites) as favorites_remaining,\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM profiles) as profiles_remaining,\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM auth.users) as users_remaining;\n```\n\n**Expected output:**\n```\nstatus: \"Cleanup Complete!\"\nfavorites_remaining: 0\nprofiles_remaining: 0\nusers_remaining: 0\n```\n\n---\n\n## **How to Run:**\n\n1. Go to [Supabase Dashboard](https://supabase.com)\n2. Select your project\n3. Click **\"SQL Editor\"** in left sidebar\n4. Click **\"New query\"**\n5. Copy and paste the **Complete Fresh Start Script** above\n6. Click **\"Run\"** (or press `Ctrl+Enter`)\n7. Verify all counts are `0`\n\n---\n\n## **After Cleanup:**\n\n1. ✅ Database is completely empty\n2. ✅ No users exist\n3. ✅ No favorites exist\n4. ✅ No profiles exist\n5. ✅ Ready for fresh signup\n\n**Next:** Open your app and create a new account to test!\n\n---\n\n**Note:** The trigger will automatically create a profile when you sign up with the new account."
