    "Perfect! I've completed a comprehensive analysis of your StreamWatch mobile app. Let me provide you with a complete understanding:\n\n## **StreamWatch Mobile App - Complete Analysis**\n\n### **Project Overview**\nStreamWatch is a React Native mobile app built with Expo that allows users to monitor, organize, and stream live content from multiple platforms (Twitch, YouTube, Kick, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, and 15+ more).\n\n### **Tech Stack**\n- **Framework**: React Native 0.81.5 with Expo SDK 54\n- **Language**: TypeScript\n- **Navigation**: React Navigation (Bottom Tabs + Native Stack)\n- **Backend**: Python API (Railway) + Supabase (PostgreSQL)\n- **Video Player**: expo-video\n- **State Management**: React Context API\n- **Authentication**: Supabase Auth (email/password + anonymous)\n- **Storage**: AsyncStorage + Supabase\n\n### **Architecture**\n\n**Core Structure:**\n```\nsrc/\n├── screens/          # 6 main screens\n│   ├── AuthScreen.tsx       # Login/signup/guest\n│   ├── HomeScreen.tsx       # Live streams only\n│   ├── LibraryScreen.tsx    # All favorites (online/offline)\n│   ├── AddScreen.tsx        # Add new streams\n│   ├── PlayerScreen.tsx     # Video player with quality selector\n│   └── SettingsScreen.tsx   # App info & logout\n├── components/\n│   ├── StreamCard.tsx       # Reusable stream card\n│   └── CustomSplashScreen.tsx\n├── context/\n│   └── StreamContext.tsx    # Global stream state\n├── hooks/\n│   └── useStreamResolver.ts # Stream resolution logic\n├── services/\n│   └── engine.ts           # API communication\n├── types/\n│   └── index.ts            # TypeScript interfaces\n└── theme/\n    └── Theme.ts            # Design system\n```\n\n### **Key Features**\n\n1. **Multi-Platform Support**: 20+ streaming platforms\n2. **Live Status Monitoring**: Real-time online/offline detection\n3. **Smart Caching**: Backend caches stream metadata (indicated by ⚡)\n4. **Quality Selection**: Multiple stream quality options\n5. **Batch Status Checks**: Efficient API calls for multiple streams\n6. **Platform-Specific UI**: Color-coded platform badges\n7. **Guest Mode**: Anonymous authentication\n8. **Favorites Management**: Add/delete streams from library\n\n### **Data Flow**\n\n1. **Authentication** → Supabase Auth\n2. **User adds stream** → Stored in Supabase `favorites` table\n3. **App fetches favorites** → StreamContext loads user's streams\n4. **Status check** → Python API `/status-batch` endpoint\n5. **Stream resolution** → Python API `/resolve` endpoint (uses yt-dlp/streamlink)\n6. **Video playback** → expo-video with quality URLs\n\n### **API Integration**\n\n**Backend URL**: `https://streamwatch-api-production.up.railway.app`\n\n**Endpoints:**\n- `POST /status-batch` - Check multiple streams (with cache support)\n- `GET /resolve?url={url}` - Resolve stream URLs and qualities\n- Both support `bypass_cache=true` parameter\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- 400: Invalid request\n- 404: Stream not found\n- 422: Unsupported platform/plugin error\n- 429: Rate limiting (includes retry_after)\n- 503: Service unavailable\n\n### **Database Schema (Supabase)**\n\n```sql\nfavorites table:\n- id (primary key)\n- user_id (foreign key to auth.users)\n- streamer_name (text)\n- original_url (text)\n- created_at (timestamp)\n```\n\n### **Design System**\n\n**Color Palette:**\n- Background: `#0A0A0A` (pure black)\n- Card: `#161616` (dark gray)\n- Primary: `#2B35FF` (electric blue)\n- Live: `#10B981` (emerald green)\n- Accent: `#00D1FF` (cyan)\n\n**Platform Colors**: Each platform has a unique brand color (Twitch purple, YouTube red, Kick green, etc.)\n\n### **Current State & Recent Updates**\n\nBased on the docs folder, recent implementations include:\n1. ✅ Custom splash screen with branding\n2. ✅ Cache awareness indicators (⚡ badge)\n3. ✅ Library shows all streams (not just live)\n4. ✅ Thumbnail fallback handling\n5. ✅ Enhanced error handling with HTTP status codes\n\n### **Environment Variables**\n```\nEXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL