    "I'll analyze the requirements and recommend an approach for adding forgot password functionality and username support.\n\n## Analysis\n\n### Current State\n- **Auth**: Supabase Auth with email/password\n- **User Data**: Only `user_id` stored in `favorites` table\n- **No username field** in current implementation\n- **No password reset flow**\n\n### Requirements\n1. Forgot password screen + flow\n2. Username field for signup/signin\n3. Store and retrieve username\n\n## Recommended Approach\n\n### **Option 1: Supabase Auth Metadata (Recommended)**\n**Pros:**\n- No schema changes needed\n- Username stored in `auth.users.raw_user_meta_data`\n- Built-in password reset via Supabase\n- Simplest implementation\n\n**Cons:**\n- Username not easily queryable for \"find by username\" features\n- Metadata is JSON, less structured\n\n### **Option 2: Separate Profiles Table**\n**Pros:**\n- Structured data with indexes\n- Can add more profile fields later\n- Username searchable/unique constraint possible\n\n**Cons:**\n- Requires database migration\n- More complex (trigger/RPC for user creation)\n- Overkill for just username\n\n### **Option 3: Hybrid Approach (Best for Scale)**\n**Pros:**\n- Username in metadata for quick access\n- Profiles table for extended data\n- Flexible for future features\n\n**Cons:**\n- Most complex initially\n\n---\n\n## **My Recommendation: Option 1 + Profiles Table**\n\nHere's why:\n1. **Username in metadata** - Quick to implement, available immediately after signup\n2. **Add profiles table** - Future-proof for avatar, bio, preferences, etc.\n3. **Supabase password reset** - Built-in, secure, email-based\n\n### Implementation Plan\n\n#### **1. Database Changes**\n```sql\n-- Create profiles table\nCREATE TABLE profiles (\n  id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id) PRIMARY KEY,\n  username TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),\n  updated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- Enable RLS\nALTER TABLE profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\n-- Policy: Users can read all profiles\nCREATE POLICY \"Profiles are viewable by everyone\"\n  ON profiles FOR SELECT\n  USING (true);\n\n-- Policy: Users can update their own profile\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can update own profile\"\n  ON profiles FOR UPDATE\n  USING (auth.uid() = id);\n\n-- Function to create profile on signup\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()\nRETURNS TRIGGER AS $$\nBEGIN\n  INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, username)\n  VALUES (\n    NEW.id,\n    COALESCE(NEW.raw_user_meta_data->>'username', 'user_' || substr(NEW.id::text, 1, 8))\n  );\n  RETURN NEW;\nEND;\n$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER;\n\n-- Trigger to auto-create profile\nCREATE TRIGGER on_auth_user_created\n  AFTER INSERT ON auth.users\n  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user();\n```\n\n#### **2. Auth Flow Changes**\n\n**Signup:**\n```typescript\nconst { data, error } = await supabase.auth.signUp({\n  email,\n  password,\n  options: {\n    data: { username } // Stored in metadata\n  }\n});\n```\n\n**Password Reset:**\n```typescript\n// Request reset\nawait supabase.auth.resetPasswordForEmail(email, {\n  redirectTo: 'streamwatch://reset-password'\n});\n\n// Update password (after email link)\nawait supabase.auth.updateUser({ password: newPassword });\n```\n\n**Get Username:**\n```typescript\nconst { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();\nconst username = user?.user_metadata?.username;\n\n// OR from profiles table\nconst { data: profile } = await supabase\n  .from('profiles')\n  .select('username')\n  .eq('id', user.id)\n  .single();\n```\n\n#### **3. UI Changes**\n\n**New Screens:**\n- `ForgotPasswordScreen.tsx` - Email input → send reset link\n- `ResetPasswordScreen.tsx` - New password input (deep link handler)\n\n**Modified Screens:**\n- `AuthScreen.tsx` - Add username field to signup, \"Forgot Password?\" link to login\n\n#### **4. Deep Linking Setup**\n```json\n// app.json\n{\n  \"expo\": {\n    \"scheme\": \"streamwatch\",\n    \"ios\": {\n      \"associatedDomains\": [\"applinks:lnuxpkwnbesqrqsxyiek.supabase.co\"]\n    },\n    \"android\": {\n      \"intentFilters\": [...]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Minimal Implementation Steps\n\n1. **Database**: Run SQL migration in Supabase dashboard\n2. **Add username to signup** (metadata approach - no DB needed initially)\n3. **Add forgot password screen** (Supabase built-in)\n4. **Add deep link handling** for password reset\n5. **Display username** in app (from metadata)\n\n**Later (optional):** Migrate to profiles table for advanced features\n\n---\n\n## Questions for You\n\n1. **Do you want username to be unique?** (requires profiles table + validation)\n2. **Should users sign in with username OR email?** (requires profiles table lookup)\n3. **Do you need username search/discovery?** (requires profiles table with index)\n4. **Any other profile fields planned?** (avatar, bio, etc.)\n\n**If answers are mostly \"no\"**, we can start with **metadata-only** approach (fastest).\n\n**If \"yes\" to any**, we should implement **profiles table** from the start.\n\nWhich approach do you prefer? I can start implementing immediately once you decide.\n[Tool uses: none]",
